    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Defensive grind",
          "heading": "Ireland made 215 tackles beating Australia; Nick Timoney hails instant rebound",
          "body": "Friday's 38-14 win over Australia at Allianz Stadium was earned largely without the ball. The Wallabies had more than 90% possession before Jeremy Williams burrowed over for a 7-0 lead, and made only 129 tackles all night. Robbie Henshaw's try had it level within minutes, though Timoney conceded: \"It didn't come all that naturally.\" Both sides managed 11 entries to the 22; Ireland turned theirs into five tries and a penalty, the Wallabies into two."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat England 26-8 to reverse last week's defeat",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan 40-10 in Nations Championship play-off. Italy's Tommaso Menoncello needs shoulder surgery, looks set to miss Six Nations. Rory Darge returns from injury to captain Scotland against Argentina."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Tommaso Menoncello needs shoulder surgery and looks set to miss Six Nations",
          "body": "The Toulouse centre broke down in training with a recurrence of the acromioclavicular sprain he suffered against Exeter in the Champions Cup in mid-October. A month and a half of conservative treatment had brought him back to training, seemingly close to a return, before the shoulder gave way. OnRugby puts the lay-off at three to four months. Even at the short end he would return in late February or early March without match minutes, too late, the outlet reckons, to risk for the Six Nations' closing rounds."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat England 26-8 to reverse last week's defeat",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan 40-10 in Nations Championship play-off. Rory Darge returns from injury to captain Scotland against Argentina."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "OnRugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain returns",
          "heading": "Rory Darge returns from injury to captain Townsend's 11-change Scotland side",
          "body": "Darge leads a side in which only Darcy Graham, Rory Hutchinson, Jamie Dobie and Jonny Gray survive from the 67-5 rout of Japan, with Finn Russell back at fly-half for Sunday's seventh-place final against Argentina at Twickenham. With the squad's No. 8s injured, Gregor Townsend turns to Magnus Bradbury: \"I'm sure he knows it's a big opportunity for him ahead of the Six Nations.\" Townsend also revealed he considered replacement hooker Seb Stephen at No. 8 before deciding against it this weekend."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat England 26-8 to reverse last week's defeat",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan 40-10 in Nations Championship play-off. Italy's Tommaso Menoncello needs shoulder surgery, looks set to miss Six Nations."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Twickenham Stadium, London"
      },
